<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n99577" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σύναυλ-ος</span></b>  (A), <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αὐλός</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>in concert with the flute</i>; then generally,
				<i>sounding in concord</i> or <i>unison, harmonious</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ξ. ὕμνων βοά</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>Ra.</u>
					212
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.): generally, <i>in harmony with</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ξ. βοὰ Χαρᾷ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>El.</u>
					879
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὅτε τις κύκνος . . ἀνέμου σύναυλος
					ἠχῇ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>Anacreont.</u>
					60.10
				</span></i>
			.</div>
